# The read-only system is mounted from the boot file's root hash (systemd-veritysetup-generator).
# /var and the machine-id are mounted in the initrd by suveryn-boot-mode.service, not here: on the
# installed appliance /var is the encrypted data partition of the disk it started from (noexec,
# nosuid, nodev); on the installer stick it is in memory (#37). /tmp is in memory; there is no swap.
tmpfs                   /tmp  tmpfs  mode=1777,nosuid,nodev,size=25%     0 0
